WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.853
Idea. A parent loses their job, and the family struggles to buy food. What could help? Money now, to cover the basics. Or skills and good health, so the parent can earn again.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:20.833
Governments use four main tools to reduce poverty and inequality: progressive tax, benefits, education and healthcare.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:33.218
A progressive tax takes a higher percentage of income as income rises. Here the rate climbs from ten to forty per cent. It narrows the gap, and pays for services for the poor.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:42.321
Benefits raise low incomes directly. Education gives skills to get better jobs. Healthcare keeps people well enough to work.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:54.687
Method. Step one, name the measure. Step two, explain how it works: it raises income, or skills, or health. Step three, apply it to the country's data.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:04.828
Step four, for Assess or Evaluate, weigh the drawbacks. Benefits can reduce the incentive to work: the poverty trap. Every measure has a cost.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:21.979
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2024. India offers cash transfers, food rations and training courses to very low-income people. Analyse how benefits can help reduce poverty. Six marks.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:36.062
Benefits are payments or support from the government to people on low incomes. Chain one: cash transfers raise income, so families can buy food, shelter and medicine. Absolute poverty falls.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:46.366
Chain two: food rations cover the most basic need. Families spend less on food, freeing money for other needs, and better nutrition helps them work.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:02:02.801
Chain three: training gives unemployed workers new skills, so they find jobs and earn a regular wage. This tackles a cause of poverty, not just its symptoms. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:13.562
Common mistake. A common mistake is saying a progressive tax means the rich pay more money. It means they pay a higher percentage of their income.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:20.477
Another is saying benefits reduce poverty, full stop. Explain what the money lets people buy.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:34.461
Your turn. Now you try. Country N plans free school meals and a training scheme for unemployed adults. Explain how each could reduce poverty, and give one drawback. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:44.450
Answer. Free meals save families money on food, and well-fed children are healthier and learn better. That cuts poverty now, and later.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.649
Training gives adults skills, so they find jobs and earn a regular wage.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:57.922
One drawback: both cost tax money that could be spent elsewhere, an opportunity cost. And training takes time to pay off.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:08.085
Remember: name the measure, explain how it raises income, skills or health, apply it, and weigh the drawbacks. Now try the practice questions.
